There are many times in the game when you are warned before doing
something silly, like attacking a shopkeeper your your pet.  To many of
these, the "correct" answer is "no".

However, when you are getting quite full, you are asked if you wish to
stop eating, in which case the "correct" answer is usually "yes".

I (semi-seriously) submit that all the default, safe answers to warning
questions should be the same (either always "no" or always "yes").  For
instance, rather than "Stop eating?" it should say "Continue eating?",
in which case the answers would be reversed and match the rest of the
warnings.

In other words, how many times have you hit 'n' to the "Stop eating"
questions by mistake?  Or is it just me?  :)

